      "message": "fix(sim): (c3) reads a span's own floor where its lerp can lean past the samples\n\nThe exact rim dip in the mid-turn sweep assumed an in-between pose is\nnever more tilted than its more tilted sample. That holds only while\nevery A and B letter of both samples stays inside (-90, 90) degrees\n(cos θ = cos A·cos B, -ln cos convex there); past it the lerp can lean\nfurther than both samples (A 100 -> 260 passes straight down; A = B\n60 -> 120 holds 75.5 degrees at both ends and 90 between). The old\nwhole radius did not cover that either: the axial part moves too.\n\nverify::tilt_span::span_floor bounds such a span from the interval of\ncos θ the lerp can reach; each pose sample reads the lower of its own\nexact bottom and the floors of the spans it ends. Inside the cap\nnothing changes. No existing verdict moved.\n\nRefs #1303\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
